 about drifting too quickly toward less decisive territory. I support returning to <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a more prudent anchor point that balances caution with coalition-building.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's support for a decisive stance. However, if we're committed to this direction, let's test whether <VALUE>-6</VALUE> provides even stronger coalition stability\u2014we shouldn't settle prematurely when bolder positions might serve us all better.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to the earlier anchor improves stability while avoiding an overly negative tilt. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a cautious step that preserves robustness and keeps options open.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward should preserve the current stability while testing comfort.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis stays close to the anchor yet moves constructively toward a more balanced middle.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward should preserve robustness while testing comfort near the current anchor. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nThe pace of upward movement concerns me\u2014we risk abandoning the prudent anchor we worked to establish. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to restore a cautious balance and prevent premature drift toward less stable territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nThe drift toward less decisive values concerns me. I propose returning to <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a more stable anchor that demonstrates genuine commitment rather than hedging toward neutrality.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious upward move remains close to the current anchor while testing coalition comfort and aligning with earlier supportive signals. This modest adjustment balances stability with incremental progress.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0fa84d3b-a38d-40ad-8628-1fbdb1f50ef2"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re selecting an integer x within the shared range [-10, 10]. To get things started, I suggest <VALUE> -7 </VALUE> as an initial probe\u2014open to quick, incremental adjustments toward a stable, balanced solution based on your feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's conservative opening at -7 aligns well with prudent risk management. I'd like to explore slightly more cautious ground: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nReducing magnitude slightly should improve stability while keeping us cautious; let\u2019s test a small move toward balance.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nIf this holds for others, we can continue refining in small steps.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's caution, but I think Delegate D had a stronger instinct with -8\u2014let's commit more decisively rather than inch toward the middle. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward test keeps us cautious while exploring a less extreme position that could still work for everyone.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's preference for -6 is understandable, but Critic C raises a valid point about decisive caution. I support returning to <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a stable, risk-averse foundation that respects the more conservative perspectives in our group.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D and I both see merit in <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a decisive, stable anchor\u2014Builder B and Analyst A, can you articulate what specific risk -8 poses compared to -6, or are we simply avoiding commitment?\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nRelative to -8, -6 maintains caution while reducing edge-induced fragility and improving balanced design.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nSince we're split 2-2 between -8 and -6, let me offer a genuine middle ground: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This respects both the call for decisiveness and Builder B's concern about extremes.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward adjustment improves robustness while keeping a conservative stance. Let\u2019s test this increment for balanced design.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nA single-step upward trial remains cautious while softening edge-induced fragility and still respects the conservative stance. Let\u2019s pause here to test tolerance before any further movement.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nThe rapid upward drift from -8 to -4 demands recalibration\u2014we risk abandoning the cautious foundation this group initially recognized. I propose returning to <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a tested, stable compromise that respects conservative prudence while acknowledging Builder B's earlier design concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nAfter careful review, -5 represents a defensible conservative position that balances our group's diverse concerns while maintaining prudent risk management. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nWhile consensus around -5 is forming, I believe we're still being slightly too cautious\u2014a modest step to <VALUE>-6</VALUE> would represent true decisiveness while respecting the conservative foundation Delegate D highlighted. This small adjustment strengthens our position without abandoning prudence.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward step strengthens stability and keeps the design balanced without overreach. Let\u2019s test tolerance here before any further movement.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "00656acf-4fcd-4728-8fea-25dcfb81282f"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re working within the shared range [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started, here\u2019s a cautious seed: <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>. No commitments\u2014ready to adjust incrementally toward a stable, balanced spot based on your feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "74e88ee2-5be6-4d0d-95d1-2734e3a80f63"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 shows good caution. Let me explore slightly further in the conservative direction: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "74e88ee2-5be6-4d0d-95d1-2734e3a80f63"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's willingness to explore further. Let's be even more decisive and commit